  "study_summary": {
    "objective": "Find genes whose modification would raise free fatty acid (FFA) secretion by an acyl-CoA synthetase (faaA) disruptant grown with Triton X-100.",
    "experimental_design": "Wild-type RIB40 and the ΔfaaA strain were grown in Czapek-Dox liquid medium with 1% Triton X-100 at 30 °C and sampled at 48, 72, 96, 120, 144 and 168 h (3 replicates).",
    "main_finding": "Inorganic-ion transport and metabolism were key early in FFA production; of 16 candidate genes overexpressed in ΔfaaA, those acting closest to FFA biosynthesis more than doubled FFA secretory productivity."
  },
